      violating conduct; and all costs of investigation and enforcement.

  (b) STATUTORY AND OTHER RELIEF. Unauthorized copying, distribution, or
      modification of the Software also constitutes copyright infringement and,
      where applicable, misappropriation of trade secrets and breach of
      contract. Licensor may pursue all remedies available at law and in
      equity, cumulatively and not alternatively, including statutory damages
      and enhanced damages for willful infringement.

  (c) LIQUIDATED DAMAGES. Because the harm from unauthorized redistribution or
      modification is difficult to quantify precisely, You agree that for each
      unauthorized copy conveyed to a third party, and for each derivative work
      created or distributed, You shall pay Licensor as liquidated damages, and
      not as a penalty, the greater of (i) five thousand U.S. dollars
      (USD $5,000) or (ii) Licensor's then-current list price for the Software
      multiplied by the number of persons or devices that received or could
      access the unauthorized copy or derivative work. The parties agree this
      amount is a reasonable pre-estimate of Licensor's loss. Liquidated damages
      under this subsection are in lieu of actual damages for the same copies,
      at Licensor's election.

  (d) INJUNCTIVE RELIEF. A breach of Section 2 or Section 3 causes irreparable
      harm for which monetary damages alone are inadequate. Licensor is
      entitled to immediate injunctive and other equitable relief without the
      requirement to post bond or prove actual damages.

  (e) COSTS AND FEES. You shall reimburse Licensor for all reasonable
      attorneys' fees, expert fees, and costs incurred in enforcing this
      Agreement, in any action in which Licensor substantially prevails.

  (f) AUDIT. Upon reasonable notice and not more than once per twelve (12)
      months absent suspected breach, Licensor may audit Your use of the
      Software to verify compliance. If an audit reveals underpayment or
      unlicensed use, You shall pay the shortfall plus the cost of the audit.

  (g) INDEMNITY. You shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless Licensor and
      its officers, employees, and agents from and against any claim, loss,
      liability, or expense arising out of Your breach of this Agreement or
      Your use of the Software.

